\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces One uplink TB in one 180\nonbreakingspace ms period of our test timeline, which is slower than 5G slot timing. Until the 45\nonbreakingspace ms NeuralRx\xspace  deadline, the TB has a pending recovery that no GPU queue contains. If the NeuralRx\xspace  result fails, is late, or is missing, one cuPHY recovery must finish before the 153\nonbreakingspace ms recovery deadline.}}{3}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:airan-background}{{1}{3}{One uplink TB in one 180~ms period of our test timeline, which is slower than 5G slot timing. Until the 45~ms \NRx deadline, the TB has a pending recovery that no GPU queue contains. If the \NRx result fails, is late, or is missing, one cuPHY recovery must finish before the 153~ms recovery deadline}{figure.caption.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The number of recoveries that a period needs is hard to predict. (a) Share of TBs that NeuralRx\xspace  (solid) and the conventional receiver (dashed) decode in three channels: a synthetic fading channel without a direct path (block Rayleigh) and two 3GPP channels with a direct path (CDL-D) and a strong direct path (CDL-E); 0\nonbreakingspace dB is where the conventional receiver decodes half of the TBs. (b) Probability that one or more, two or more, three or more, or all four TBs of a period fail when each TB fails with probability $p$. Lines assume independent failures; the band shows the all-four event with a correlation of 0.3. Circles are measured periods, and squares are groups of four measured receiver trials.}}{3}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:debt}{{2}{3}{The number of recoveries that a period needs is hard to predict. (a) Share of TBs that \NRx (solid) and the conventional receiver (dashed) decode in three channels: a synthetic fading channel without a direct path (block Rayleigh) and two 3GPP channels with a direct path (CDL-D) and a strong direct path (CDL-E); 0~dB is where the conventional receiver decodes half of the TBs. (b) Probability that one or more, two or more, three or more, or all four TBs of a period fail when each TB fails with probability $p$. Lines assume independent failures; the band shows the all-four event with a correlation of 0.3. Circles are measured periods, and squares are groups of four measured receiver trials}{figure.caption.4}{}}
