\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces AI service and radio safety under bursty AI arrivals on the physical four-GPU path. Every pattern carries the same 329 BurstGPT prompts at 3 requests/s for 108\nonbreakingspace s and differs only in arrival times; the AI SLO is 200\nonbreakingspace ms. (a) AI tokens served within their SLO; idle-time admission serves the most only because it breaks the recovery deadline in (b), and static reservation admits no AI request. (b) Periods in which the admitted AI breaks the recovery deadline at the declared bounds (lines, measured service times), and periods whose last recovery actually ends after the recovery deadline when every AI request and recovery takes its full bound (padded runs). (c) Gain of Backstop\xspace  over recovery-first against the AI SLO: replay mean over the six patterns with its range (band), and the measured runs at 200\nonbreakingspace ms.}}{19}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:eval-burst}{{13}{19}{AI service and radio safety under bursty AI arrivals on the physical four-GPU path. Every pattern carries the same 329 BurstGPT prompts at 3 requests/s for 108~s and differs only in arrival times; the AI SLO is 200~ms. (a) AI tokens served within their SLO; idle-time admission serves the most only because it breaks the recovery deadline in (b), and static reservation admits no AI request. (b) Periods in which the admitted AI breaks the recovery deadline at the declared bounds (lines, measured service times), and periods whose last recovery actually ends after the recovery deadline when every AI request and recovery takes its full bound (padded runs). (c) Gain of \sys over recovery-first against the AI SLO: replay mean over the six patterns with its range (band), and the measured runs at 200~ms}{figure.caption.19}{}}
