\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces Are rejected requests really unsafe? Two nodes. (a) End of the last recovery in every attempt of the bound-padded test. E4 offers a 256-token request with two needed recoveries at 45\nonbreakingspace ms; E6b and E6a offer a 64-token request with one needed recovery at 89 and 88\nonbreakingspace ms. The other policies launch the request anyway: idle-time admission in E4 and a forced launch of the request that Backstop\xspace  rejects in E6b. (b) AI requests per prompt length in the two-node campaign: requests that Backstop\xspace  runs and requests that it rejects because the needed recoveries would then miss the recovery deadline; idle-time admission would run all of them, and static reservation runs none.}}{22}{figure.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
