\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {18}{\ignorespaces Three checks of the runtime safeguards on physical GPUs. (a) Latest start time: arrival of each AI slot at the Qwen worker relative to its latest start time, for the 1,077 slots of the two-node campaign and the 52 slots that a fault holds past it. (b) Cost of putting AI first: commit time of every recovered TB, grouped by the prompt length of the AI slot that runs before its recovery; the dotted line marks the median commit of the TBs that NeuralRx\xspace  decodes. (c) Faults: commit time of every TB under each injected fault: no fault, all TBs of a period fail, stale and duplicate NeuralRx\xspace  results, a late AI reply after the GPU finished, an AI slot held past its latest start time, an AI channel lost before the GPU finished, and stale and duplicate recovery responses.}}{23}{figure.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:eval-refinement}{{18}{23}{Three checks of the runtime safeguards on physical GPUs. (a) Latest start time: arrival of each AI slot at the Qwen worker relative to its latest start time, for the 1,077 slots of the two-node campaign and the 52 slots that a fault holds past it. (b) Cost of putting AI first: commit time of every recovered TB, grouped by the prompt length of the AI slot that runs before its recovery; the dotted line marks the median commit of the TBs that \NRx decodes. (c) Faults: commit time of every TB under each injected fault: no fault, all TBs of a period fail, stale and duplicate \NRx results, a late AI reply after the GPU finished, an AI slot held past its latest start time, an AI channel lost before the GPU finished, and stale and duplicate recovery responses}{figure.caption.24}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {19}{\ignorespaces Prediction and decision cost. (a) Latest decision time at which one AI request of each prompt length can still be admitted, with four admitted TBs and zero to four pending recoveries; circles and crosses mark the physical tests, fixed in advance, that the scheduler admitted and rejected, labeled with their prompt length. (b) Time to build and to check a candidate against the number of pending recoveries, with the 5\nonbreakingspace ms launch budget. The times are measured on finite runs, not WCETs.}}{24}{figure.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:envelope}{{19}{24}{Prediction and decision cost. (a) Latest decision time at which one AI request of each prompt length can still be admitted, with four admitted TBs and zero to four pending recoveries; circles and crosses mark the physical tests, fixed in advance, that the scheduler admitted and rejected, labeled with their prompt length. (b) Time to build and to check a candidate against the number of pending recoveries, with the 5~ms launch budget. The times are measured on finite runs, not WCETs}{figure.caption.25}{}}
